Package: shoji
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Kunal Kushwaha <kunalkushwaha@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= @GLIBC@), libwpewebkit-2.0-1 (>= 2.54), libgles2, libpng16-16t64, zlib1g, shared-mime-info
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core, bubblewrap
Suggests: fonts-noto-cjk
Section: web
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/kunalkushwaha/shoji
Description: real web browser in your terminal, drawn by WebKit (no Chrome)
 shoji renders pages with WPE WebKit off-screen and shows them in terminals that
 speak the kitty graphics protocol (Ghostty, kitty, WezTerm), inside Neovim, or
 headless for coding agents, which drive it with `shoji ctl` (snapshot, click,
 fill, eval, screenshot, console, network). Needs WPE WebKit 2.54 or newer
 (Debian testing/sid).
